00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:08.980
Let me tell you a little bit
about how we select winners and

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:11.420
let me tell you about why
we selected Ali Baba.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:16.310
So each year the company picks
a company which has distinguished

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:21.820
itself in creating and fostering
entrepreneurial spirit beyond all others.

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:25.580
We look for companies that invent and
reinvent themselves and industries.

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:29.510
We look for global leaders in important
places that shape landscapes.

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:34.250
And we look for leadership teams where
founders continue to drive achievement and

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:36.070
our entrepenarial spirit.

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:38.099
And we think Alibaba does all that and
more.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:43.200
Alibaba group was founded in 1999 and
headquartered in Hangzhou,

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:47.290
China is the worlds largest online and
mobile commerce company.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.650
Its mission is to make it easy
to do business anywhere and

00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:53.960
its certainly done that and
on a massive scale.

00:03:54.970 --> 00:04:00.850
As you'll hear Alibaba has 10 million
active sellers on the platform and

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:04.850
367 million active buyers which is
more than the population of the US and

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:05.490
Canada combined.

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:10.960
In the last fiscal year, the GMV and the
Alibaba was almost $400 billion dollars,

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:16.445
up 46% from the year prior, and
a fun few facts that I recently learned.

00:04:16.445 --> 00:04:22.940
86% of all goods purchased on mobile
phones in China were done on Alibaba.

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:27.645
They created Singles Day which
is celebrated on November 11th,

00:04:27.645 --> 00:04:31.860
1-1-1-1, which is now the world's
largest shopping day.

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:37.530
In a single 24 hour period, Alibaba saw
9.3 billion sales which is more than 3 and

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:41.420
a half times the total E-commerce
sales in the US on Black Friday and

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:42.700
Cyber Monday combined.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:48.830
On an average day, 30 million Alibaba
packages are delivered which is more

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:53.670
than the largest day the United States
Postal Service ever experienced, and

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:59.090
last September the company debuted the
largest IPO in the world at $25 billion.

00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:03.740
So there's a lot of largest and
biggest which is pretty impressive for

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:07.130
a company that is still very young and
innovative.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:12.660
And finally, it's founder, Jack Ma,
is widely considered one of the most

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:17.000
innovative and thoughtful entrepreneurs
in the world today or possibly ever.

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:19.660
So why do we pick Alibaba?

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:22.520
That's why.

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:28.470
Tonight we're very fortunate to have Jack
interviewed by our mutual good friend and

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:31.530
renowned internet entrepreneur Jerry Yang.

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:36.160
Jerry needs little introduction but
deserves this and much more.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:40.900
He's a Stanford BS and MS grad and
co-founded Yahoo in 1995 while working on

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:47.279
his PhD at Stanford and we wonder, along
with his mother, if he'll ever finish.

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:52.890
He served in various management roles,
including CEO and Chief Yahoo and

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:54.990
as a board member until 2012.

00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:59.910
Among other things, he also led Yahoo's
investment, now famous investment Alibaba,

00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:02.830
which I hope he'll discuss
at some point tonight.

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:07.270
Jerry has served as a Director
of Yahoo and Cisco,

00:06:07.270 --> 00:06:12.075
and currently serves on the boards
of Workday, Lenovo, and Alibaba.

00:06:12.075 --> 00:06:16.632
He and his wife Akiko are well known
philanthropists and generous benefactors

00:06:16.632 --> 00:06:21.546
to Stanford where he recently retired from
the board of directors and as vice chair.

00:06:21.546 --> 00:06:25.984
Jerry and I have been friends for more
than 20 years, and if I had a dollar for

00:06:25.984 --> 00:06:30.600
every time someone called me Jerry,
I too would donate a building to Stanford.

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:33.273
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Please join me in welcoming Jerry Yang.

00:06:33.273 --> 00:06:42.756
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

00:06:42.756 --> 00:06:44.573
&gt;&gt; Thank you Jeff.

00:06:44.573 --> 00:06:48.478
It's my honor to be here and
to introduce the founder and

00:06:48.478 --> 00:06:51.670
executive chairman of Alibaba Group.

00:06:51.670 --> 00:06:52.970
My friend Jack Ma.

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:58.285
As Jack likes to say himself,
he's 100% made in China.

00:06:58.285 --> 00:07:03.170
[LAUGH] But his story embodies
very much the American dream.

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:05.910
An English teacher with little means and

00:07:05.910 --> 00:07:09.430
no connections,
Jack built Alibaba from the ground up.

00:07:09.430 --> 00:07:12.280
He was born in Hungo.

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:17.860
The Chinese city that was made
famous by Nixon's visit in 1972.

00:07:17.860 --> 00:07:22.417
And he learned English by riding his
bike to a hotel, I didn't know this,

00:07:22.417 --> 00:07:27.654
every day for nine years and volunteering
as a tour guide practicing with tourists.

00:07:27.654 --> 00:07:33.722
Then on his first trip to the US, 20 years
ago in 1995, Jack first saw the internet

00:07:33.722 --> 00:07:38.888
and realized the potential to connect
people within and outside of China.

00:07:38.888 --> 00:07:45.314
He founded Alibaba with a group of
friends in his apartment in 1999.

00:07:45.314 --> 00:07:49.475
&gt;From the beginning Jack and his
co-founders shared a focus on the small

00:07:49.475 --> 00:07:52.055
business and entrepreneurial community.

00:07:52.055 --> 00:07:57.440
It was their collective belief
that by leveraging technology

00:07:57.440 --> 00:08:03.558
it will bring small businesses
Across China into the global economy.

00:08:03.558 --> 00:08:09.091
Now Jack is an unlikely tech
entrepreneur in that he openly admits

00:08:09.091 --> 00:08:16.148
he's never written a line of code, but he
is a visionary in every sense of the word.

00:08:16.148 --> 00:08:19.430
In just fifteen years,
Alibaba has become the largest online and

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:21.828
mobile commerce company,
as Jeff mentioned.

00:08:21.828 --> 00:08:26.936
And not even Jack could have predicted
the change he would bring to China.

00:08:26.936 --> 00:08:30.623
Creating jobs and prosperity for
millions in the urban and rural China,

00:08:30.623 --> 00:08:34.620
empowering millions of entrepreneurs and
changing the way that people live.

00:08:37.090 --> 00:08:40.645
Not only live, but shop and
work online in China.

00:08:40.645 --> 00:08:44.313
And before I bring Jack up,
we're going to run a brief video.

00:08:44.313 --> 00:08:45.173
