the others.

00:14:45.827 --> 00:14:48.381
But there is a lot of
a misunderstanding between us.

00:14:48.381 --> 00:14:54.830
And my suggestion is that US and China
should nod like chicken talks to ducks.

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:57.480
Everybody want to tell, nobody listen.

00:14:57.480 --> 00:15:00.460
We need a common language
between chick and ducks, right?

00:15:00.460 --> 00:15:02.621
People talk the same language,
we have the same standard.

00:15:02.621 --> 00:15:07.218
And I think this kind of dialog's

00:15:07.218 --> 00:15:11.492
pretty effective and useful.

00:15:11.492 --> 00:15:14.522
And I suggested that we
should have a US and

00:15:14.522 --> 00:15:18.660
China business dialog talk annually,
every year.

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:20.430
Once in America, once in China.

00:15:20.430 --> 00:15:22.900
Get the government leaders sitting there,
and

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:25.080
how can improve the business environment.

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:28.090
Normally government leaders have
a lot of a dispute argue, but

00:15:28.090 --> 00:15:31.100
business people, we talk a lot.

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:32.988
If we don't talk, will be problems.

00:15:32.988 --> 00:15:37.446
So I think the Seattle trip is good.

00:15:37.446 --> 00:15:38.421
&gt;&gt; Yeah?
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:15:38.421 --> 00:15:42.810
&gt;&gt; Good, I'm surprised you
even answered my question.

00:15:42.810 --> 00:15:43.367
That's good.

00:15:43.367 --> 00:15:47.222
Usually he'll just talk about
whatever he wants to talk about.

00:15:47.222 --> 00:15:47.779
So thank you.

00:15:47.779 --> 00:15:52.662
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; I try to talk the ducks language,

00:15:52.662 --> 00:15:53.230
you know?

00:15:53.230 --> 00:15:58.226
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; The Chinese

00:15:58.226 --> 00:16:02.270
economy has been on everybody's mind.

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:07.820
I mean and
people are worried here that the slowdown

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:11.963
in China will affect global economy.

00:16:11.963 --> 00:16:13.830
How are you seeing things?

00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:14.820
I mean, obviously,

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:18.178
the stock market has been kind of
a symbol of something that's a bubble.

00:16:18.178 --> 00:16:22.880
But what is going on in China from your
viewpoint, what's your perspective?

00:16:22.880 --> 00:16:25.625
I mean, you're not an economist,
but you see so much going on there.

00:16:25.625 --> 00:16:32.260
&gt;&gt; Yeah, well, first, I think people in
the states in the west worry about China.

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:36.280
I think it's a good thing, because
every time when west worry about China,

00:16:36.280 --> 00:16:37.020
China go up.

00:16:37.020 --> 00:16:41.132
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; And when people in the western think,

00:16:41.132 --> 00:16:45.999
wow, Chinese has a good future and
Chinese has a problem and

00:16:45.999 --> 00:16:53.670
the western has been suspect Chinese
growth for past 30 years, so that is fine.

00:16:53.670 --> 00:16:57.720
It takes time for
both side to understand each other.

00:16:57.720 --> 00:17:03.143
China I think keep on growing for
10, 11, 12% for so many years.

00:17:03.143 --> 00:17:07.183
I don't think can last long and
it's impossible like a side effect,

00:17:07.183 --> 00:17:09.760
it's like a human body when you are 1.2,

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:14.590
1.8 meters tall, you cannot keep
growing at that pace all the time.

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:19.990
You have to keep growing your quality,
the brain not the body size.

00:17:19.990 --> 00:17:24.324
And especially today, I don't think first,
it's impossible to keep 10, 15,

00:17:24.324 --> 00:17:25.780
11% of growth annually.

00:17:25.780 --> 00:17:32.588
Secondly is that China needed to be slowed
down, it had to learn to be slowed down.

00:17:32.588 --> 00:17:35.757
because when you see the water,
when you see the air,

00:17:35.757 --> 00:17:41.034
when you see all the resources we used,
it's impossible and it's ridiculous.

00:17:41.034 --> 00:17:45.106
China making a lot of money and
we spend the money on the medicine and

00:17:45.106 --> 00:17:48.630
spend the money on the hospital,
this can not work.

00:17:48.630 --> 00:17:54.138
So on the other side, people like me,
I think China is slowing down for 7%.

00:17:54.138 --> 00:17:58.263
Good and but the thing,
even 7%, think about,

00:17:58.263 --> 00:18:02.516
we are still the fastest
gross economy in the year.

00:18:02.516 --> 00:18:08.486
With the 7% of the total GDP, think
about it guys, this is lots of money.

00:18:08.486 --> 00:18:12.910
We should use the money in a better way,
we need quality not quantity.

00:18:12.910 --> 00:18:16.379
30 years ago, we needed a lot of quantity,
but now it's quality.

00:18:16.379 --> 00:18:20.883
So, I think in the west have a high
expectation that China should have

00:18:20.883 --> 00:18:21.700
quality.

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:25.877
China should control the air and
the pollution and this and then.

00:18:25.877 --> 00:18:28.160
When we really start to do it,
people start to worry.

00:18:29.560 --> 00:18:31.870
Which is fine, but this is slowing down.

00:18:31.870 --> 00:18:34.889
On the other thing is that I think
China economy is not that bad.

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:38.760
There are two things.

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:43.140
There are three called three marks, horse.

00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:43.705
&gt;&gt; Carriages.

00:18:43.705 --> 00:18:49.680
&gt;&gt; Carriages, investment infrastructure,
exporting, domestic consumptions.

00:18:49.680 --> 00:18:52.380
These are the three things
that China's always proud of,

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:54.959
that these are the three engines
that put China economy grow.

00:18:56.180 --> 00:18:59.540
But the investment of infrastructure,
slowing down.

00:19:01.140 --> 00:19:03.990
And exporting, slowing down.

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:07.180
These are the two things government
is very good at, they love do it,

00:19:07.180 --> 00:19:11.160
because they have the power
to exporting and investment.

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:15.668
But there's one thing they could not do
it in a good way is the consumptions,

00:19:15.668 --> 00:19:18.980
because consumption is not
determined by government,

00:19:18.980 --> 00:19:23.149
consumption is determined by
entrepreneurship and market economy.

00:19:23.149 --> 00:19:27.096
So I think people,
like us have to create opportunity.

00:19:27.096 --> 00:19:30.100
Now it's our turn, not government's turn.

00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:34.900
After 30 years, government
pushed the economy in their way.

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:36.770
And now, it's our way.

00:19:36.770 --> 00:19:41.900
So I considered this as opportunity for
real market economy and

00:19:41.900 --> 00:19:47.609
the next thing I said yesterday on
a conference to the dialogue, there

00:19:47.609 --> 00:19:54.315
are a lot of misunderstanding culture
difference between American and Chinese.

00:19:54.315 --> 00:19:57.499
When Americans think about
economies slowing down,

00:19:57.499 --> 00:20:00.265
that means people don't
have money to spend.

00:20:00.265 --> 00:20:05.499
Other guy's different, you guys
know how to spend tomorrows money.

00:20:05.499 --> 00:20:10.244
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Future's money or other people's money.

00:20:10.244 --> 00:20:13.882
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; But we Chinese,

00:20:13.882 --> 00:20:16.430
our habit is to save money.

00:20:17.530 --> 00:20:21.580
We always keep the money in the banks.

00:20:21.580 --> 00:20:23.590
China has been poor for so many years.

00:20:23.590 --> 00:20:25.859
So we worry, when we have money,
we put it in the bank.

00:20:25.859 --> 00:20:29.850
When we have money, we put it in the bank,
because we know tough days are coming.

00:20:29.850 --> 00:20:37.060
So you see, China has the largest
banking deposit in the whole world.

00:20:37.060 --> 00:20:38.931
We also deposit a lot
of money in the states.

00:20:38.931 --> 00:20:42.949
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; When we know when the tough day comes,

00:20:42.949 --> 00:20:45.560
we start to pay, we start to buy.

00:20:45.560 --> 00:20:50.075
Now the tough day comes,
people still start to buy.

00:20:50.075 --> 00:20:53.051
With our numbers shows on our website,

00:20:53.051 --> 00:20:57.930
we are the largest of 12%
the total China retailer.

00:20:57.930 --> 00:21:02.060
The consumption is still going
up healthy and aggressively,

00:21:02.060 --> 00:21:06.799
especially the economy's bad people start
to buy online because it's cheaper.

00:21:08.440 --> 00:21:13.070
The other difference, my grandmother
has only one shirt in her robe.

00:21:14.650 --> 00:21:19.527
My mother has three,
my daughter's generation, 50.

00:21:19.527 --> 00:21:26.684
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; And 48% of them should never wear it.

00:21:26.684 --> 00:21:30.041
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; This is called domestic consumption.

00:21:30.041 --> 00:21:34.238
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; And we have to put up with this kind

00:21:34.238 --> 00:21:38.979
of behavior and make people start to
spend money and this is something

00:21:38.979 --> 00:21:43.736
the government is not good at,
we know how to make this thing happen.

00:21:43.736 --> 00:21:47.280
So I think generally, I'm positive.

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:50.048
But next two or three years,
maybe have problems.

00:21:50.048 --> 00:21:56.245
People say, well, anti-corruption,
but think about anti-corruption and

00:21:56.245 --> 00:22:01.300
rule by law is laying a great
foundation for the market economy.

00:22:01.300 --> 00:22:05.287
You don't want to go do
business by bribery,

00:22:05.287 --> 00:22:10.262
you don't want to have
an unfair environment in China.

00:22:10.262 --> 00:22:14.513
So market economy is by rule by law and
market economy is about clear,

00:22:14.513 --> 00:22:16.630
transparent and fair.

00:22:16.630 --> 00:22:23.840
And I think this year, last year, bad,
but this is why we need entrepreneurship.

00:22:23.840 --> 00:22:27.169
This is why we need that
the businesses drive the economy.

00:22:27.169 --> 00:22:31.588
So I'm a positive and
when people worry, I'm happy.

00:22:31.588 --> 00:22:33.738
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; When people too happy I start to worry.

00:22:33.738 --> 00:22:35.930
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; And

00:22:35.930 --> 00:22:38.570
don't worry about the things
the president is worried about,

00:22:38.570 --> 00:22:44.610
worry about the things that nobody worry
about it and this is the opportunity.

00:22:44.610 --> 00:22:48.884
So I'm positive, because I'm positive,
but I'm not stupid.

00:22:48.884 --> 00:22:51.367
I know that we have problems, but

00:22:51.367 --> 00:22:55.990
we have to solve the problems
little by little and that's it.

00:22:55.990 --> 00:22:59.355
&gt;&gt; I think you're right in that for
a consumption and

00:22:59.355 --> 00:23:03.770
a service economy to take off and
drive China as the third engine.

00:23:03.770 --> 00:23:07.882
It is going to require more businesses
rather than governmental policies.

00:23:07.882 --> 00:23:10.321
&gt;&gt; Yeah.
&gt;&gt; So I do think that's an opportunity for

00:23:10.321 --> 00:23:14.804
not just Alibaba, but you're right
in the middle of it, but everybody.

00:23:14.804 --> 00:23:17.819
&gt;&gt; Oh, by the way,
the other thing is the new economy.

00:23:17.819 --> 00:23:21.388
You see the traditional
businesses going down, but

00:23:21.388 --> 00:23:25.020
the new economy is
growing up tremendously.

00:23:25.020 --> 00:23:29.623
So not only the BAT,
we have so many wonderful

00:23:29.623 --> 00:23:35.196
startups today coming up and
that is the rising star and

00:23:35.196 --> 00:23:40.670
this is what China should go,
not keep those things.

00:23:40.670 --> 00:23:44.790
Yeah, nobody can go back to yesterday and

00:23:44.790 --> 00:23:50.453
even if you can go back to yesterday,
you don't want to.

00:23:50.453 --> 00:23:51.754
So, I think we are.

00:23:51.754 --> 00:23:54.845
&gt;&gt; Well, I mean,
my perspective from being there

00:23:54.845 --> 00:23:58.789
yesterday is that I think Both
the government leadership and

00:23:58.789 --> 00:24:04.204
especially the business communities are
emphasizing that our differences are not

00:24:04.204 --> 00:24:08.997
that big in the grand scheme of things
in that the U.S. and China are going to

00:24:08.997 --> 00:24:15.005
have to be key partners to solve
the world's problems in the next 30 years.

00:24:15.005 --> 00:24:19.375
So it is largely a collaborative effort.

00:24:19.375 --> 00:24:22.535
And I think Jackie-
&gt;&gt; Yeah, if we collaborate,

00:24:22.535 --> 00:24:26.475
we can a lot of American dreams and
Chinese dreams and world dreams.

00:24:27.715 --> 00:24:30.416
If we don't collaborate,
then we do not [INAUDIBLE].

00:24:30.416 --> 00:24:31.267
&gt;&gt; Yep.
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:24:31.267 --> 00:24:36.087
&gt;&gt; Well let's turn and, you are here
tonight because of the entrepreneurial

00:24:36.087 --> 00:24:38.240
spirit of you and your founders.

00:24:39.540 --> 00:24:44.697
And obviously when Alibaba started
it was no such thing as e-commerce.

00:24:44.697 --> 00:24:49.056
But before if, I may get,
before we get to Alibaba,

00:24:49.056 --> 00:24:52.440
you were kind of a serial entrepreneur.

00:24:54.550 --> 00:25:01.049
In fact, you also know about government
because when I first met you in 1997,

00:25:01.049 --> 00:25:05.498
you were in a government in
between startups, I guess.

00:25:05.498 --> 00:25:13.220
And you always dreamed of
creating something, and maybe

00:25:13.220 --> 00:25:17.870
you can talk a little bit about what did
you see when you were at the government.

00:25:17.870 --> 00:25:21.280
You were coming off of another start up.

00:25:21.280 --> 00:25:25.340
Everybody is very familiar with your
story, but I think that part of it was

00:25:25.340 --> 00:25:29.960
very important to you because then you
went back to Hangzhou and started Alibaba.

00:25:29.960 --> 00:25:32.910
So maybe talk about that, and
then talk about what did you end up seeing

00:25:32.910 --> 00:25:36.110
in 1999 that make you
decide that Alibaba was it.

00:25:36.110 --> 00:25:37.960
&gt;&gt; Yeah, okay, good.

00:25:37.960 --> 00:25:43.400
Jerry knows me so well, and by the way,

00:25:43.400 --> 00:25:47.160
Jerry not only the entrepreneur and
he's a wonderful investor.

00:25:47.160 --> 00:25:49.816
Probably one of the investors right?

00:25:49.816 --> 00:25:52.415
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; I'll give you my version.

00:25:52.415 --> 00:25:54.460
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE].

00:25:54.460 --> 00:25:58.680
&gt;&gt; He's sitting under my because very
few people see the real stuff that's in

00:25:58.680 --> 00:25:59.870
his heart.

00:25:59.870 --> 00:26:01.090
He's so smart.

00:26:01.090 --> 00:26:05.780
I remember the day when we negotiated
with Yahoo, buying the Yahoo, and

00:26:05.780 --> 00:26:07.000
getting $1 billion.

00:26:07.000 --> 00:26:12.000
Today, people think it's a good deal,
but at that time, it was a big risk.

00:26:13.230 --> 00:26:14.660
It's not easy.

00:26:14.660 --> 00:26:18.160
That year,
that many years ago put $1 billion inside.

00:26:18.160 --> 00:26:22.965
And we are almost a separate carcass,
we are not happy about this and

00:26:22.965 --> 00:26:26.432
that and
at that time he wasn't the CEO, right.

00:26:26.432 --> 00:26:30.790
And then he said, we are almost
just separate then he said call me.

00:26:30.790 --> 00:26:35.720
Jack can you come and tonight we
have our drink?" For final effort.

00:26:35.720 --> 00:26:37.600
&gt;&gt; You can't drink that much back then.

00:26:37.600 --> 00:26:38.900
&gt;&gt; And then I say okay.

00:26:38.900 --> 00:26:44.125
So he took me to small, tiny Japanese
restaurant, bought me big glass of Saki.

00:26:44.125 --> 00:26:46.565
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH].

00:26:46.565 --> 00:26:50.710
&gt;&gt; And we drink and
try to convince me how wonderful Yahoo is.

00:26:50.710 --> 00:26:53.192
And after drink we say,
okay let's keep on talking good.

00:26:53.192 --> 00:26:56.392
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; The most expensive Saki I've ever had

00:26:56.392 --> 00:26:57.082
in my life.

00:26:57.082 --> 00:27:04.212
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; I'm pretty sensitive about a Saki now.

00:27:04.212 --> 00:27:05.659
&gt;&gt; I know.

00:27:05.659 --> 00:27:09.800
I was going to invite you to some
Saki after this but I guess I better.

00:27:09.800 --> 00:27:12.213
I think that-
&gt;&gt; But

00:27:12.213 --> 00:27:13.796
I will continue answer your question.

00:27:13.796 --> 00:27:15.427
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:27:15.427 --> 00:27:18.190
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH].

00:27:18.190 --> 00:27:21.640
&gt;&gt; I went back to China
with the dream of Internet.

00:27:21.640 --> 00:27:24.180
I believe this thing is
going to change the world.

00:27:24.180 --> 00:27:28.870
I believe this thing will be big,
but whether Jack Marr and

00:27:28.870 --> 00:27:30.910
his team can be successful, I don't know.

00:27:30.910 --> 00:27:34.030
I told the team somebody will
be successful, but not us.

00:27:34.030 --> 00:27:34.790
May not be us.

00:27:34.790 --> 00:27:36.932
We have to work very hard.

00:27:36.932 --> 00:27:41.587
So, tough days in China,
year 1996, 1997, and

00:27:41.587 --> 00:27:46.623
then go nowhere, because we,
only, I borrowed $2,000

00:27:46.623 --> 00:27:51.010
from my friends and families and
relatives together.

00:27:52.250 --> 00:27:54.240
So we compete with the China Telecom.

00:27:54.240 --> 00:27:57.307
They have money, they have the [INAUDIBLE]
SOE, they're state owned business.

00:27:57.307 --> 00:27:58.708
They're competing with us.

00:27:58.708 --> 00:28:03.530
Finally, they cannot kill us
because we want to survive.

00:28:03.530 --> 00:28:06.550
And we of course cannot
kill China Telecom.

00:28:06.550 --> 00:28:10.830
So we had a joint venture,
they have 70% we have 30%.

00:28:10.830 --> 00:28:13.630
And I was so
stupid I think they really love us but

00:28:13.630 --> 00:28:16.190
they got us be they want to kill us.

00:28:16.190 --> 00:28:21.440
Of five seven ball seats they got a five
two everything without even say our idea.

00:28:21.440 --> 00:28:22.700
They say they don't like it.

00:28:22.700 --> 00:28:27.160
So I say maybe I should go into Beijing.

00:28:27.160 --> 00:28:29.104
Go to Beijing, join the government,

00:28:29.104 --> 00:28:31.900
maybe they can help us in
promoting the Internet.

00:28:31.900 --> 00:28:32.882
So we want Beijing.

00:28:32.882 --> 00:28:36.459
Joined the [INAUDIBLE] Minister of
Foreign Trade, that's part of job.

00:28:36.459 --> 00:28:37.879
Contract for 14 miles.

00:28:37.879 --> 00:28:41.616
Working side of a fun
government can never,

00:28:41.616 --> 00:28:46.210
ever promote the, or
make Internet business.

00:28:46.210 --> 00:28:50.360
Because the philosophy of
Internet is try to develop,

00:28:50.360 --> 00:28:53.100
how to make other people
develop the business.

00:28:53.100 --> 00:28:55.740
But the government,
they want control at that time.

00:28:55.740 --> 00:28:57.340
So it's totally different philosophy.

00:28:57.340 --> 00:28:57.960
They are smart.

00:28:57.960 --> 00:28:58.810
They are good people, but

00:28:58.810 --> 00:29:03.570
they think how can I make it using
Internet to manage and control?

00:29:03.570 --> 00:29:08.080
But we think we should make not control,
making other people develop.

00:29:08.080 --> 00:29:11.741
So different philosophy,
I think in one works are left and

00:29:11.741 --> 00:29:14.593
during these day I met Jerry Yam,
all right.

00:29:14.593 --> 00:29:21.404
And then I think well,
no chance in the government, no chance in.

00:29:21.404 --> 00:29:24.330
I believe we should not give up.

00:29:24.330 --> 00:29:28.650
So I was in a desperate and think
a lot I should, let's go do it again.

00:29:28.650 --> 00:29:31.179
So we went back to Hangzhou.

00:29:31.179 --> 00:29:34.720
Stat, I invited 18, my students,

00:29:34.720 --> 00:29:40.266
friends in my apartment,
year 1999 February 21st.

00:29:40.266 --> 00:29:43.825
We took the video of us
talking about the future.

00:29:43.825 --> 00:29:44.615
People looked at me.

00:29:44.615 --> 00:29:45.850
This guy is crazy.

00:29:45.850 --> 00:29:47.075
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH].

00:29:47.075 --> 00:29:48.415
&gt;&gt; But most people cannot find jobs.

00:29:48.415 --> 00:29:50.085
So say what if you have
an idea let's do it.

00:29:50.085 --> 00:29:55.595
And then a good thing is
that we keep all the video.

00:29:55.595 --> 00:29:58.185
Our company probably kept
the most of the video.

00:30:00.370 --> 00:30:01.850
And most of the-
&gt;&gt; Good for you.

00:30:01.850 --> 00:30:07.040
&gt;&gt; Every meeting,
we had in the past 16 years

00:30:07.040 --> 00:30:12.370
were videotaped, because we know
everything with every mistake we made.

00:30:12.370 --> 00:30:17.970
Every decision made in the future will
give our young people to study us.

00:30:17.970 --> 00:30:22.580
We're going to open in every ten years
what happened, why we make this decision.

00:30:22.580 --> 00:30:25.620
Even discussing with Yahoo,
why we make joined with Yahoo.

00:30:25.620 --> 00:30:26.967
All videotaped.

00:30:26.967 --> 00:30:29.770
So, some day we will open it.

00:30:29.770 --> 00:30:33.260
So 1999 we started the business.

00:30:33.260 --> 00:30:37.507
And people ask,
why not a Beijing and why Hangzhou?

00:30:37.507 --> 00:30:40.420
&gt;&gt; I know Hangzhou is this
hub of entrepreneurs and

00:30:40.420 --> 00:30:44.260
start ups in tech, but back then-
&gt;&gt; Back then no where, and

00:30:44.260 --> 00:30:50.000
I think at that time Nokia was so
good, at that time.

00:30:50.000 --> 00:30:52.120
And I say, guys where's Nokia?

00:30:53.780 --> 00:30:57.130
Is a thin layer of some of small
island headquarters there.

00:30:57.130 --> 00:30:58.670
It's not where you are.

00:30:59.960 --> 00:31:04.790
I don't see, it's where your heart is,
where your vision is.

00:31:04.790 --> 00:31:10.150
So we said Beijing they love SO
you stayed on the business.

00:31:10.150 --> 00:31:13.410
Shanghai, they love
multinational companies.

00:31:13.410 --> 00:31:16.010
IBM, Microsoft, they embrace you.

00:31:16.010 --> 00:31:18.870
Startup, entrepreneur, forget it, right?

00:31:18.870 --> 00:31:22.570
So, I said if in Beijing we're nobody.

00:31:22.570 --> 00:31:24.240
In Shanghai we're nobody.

00:31:24.240 --> 00:31:27.775
If we go back to Hangzhou,
we're the only child of the local family.

00:31:27.775 --> 00:31:31.650
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Yeah, and

00:31:31.650 --> 00:31:36.750
local children are very much prized and
well taken care of, and

